<section id="how" class="part">
<h2>How to read this</h2>
<ol class="points">
<li>Times are in UTC. Your clock is one hour ahead of UTC.</li>
<li>The text gives the time of each message to the minute. In the references, a time with seconds, such as 13:00:30, names a message in the session transcript. The script show.py prints any message of yours by its time.</li>
<li>“The account” is the analysis of 28 October, in the file account.md beside this report. The evidence files are in the folder evidence beside it. The references name each file by its name and link to it.</li>
<li>A sentence that starts “My reading:” gives the judgement of this report's writer, an Opus worker. Every other sentence states what a cited source says.</li>
</ol>
<h3>Words used throughout</h3>
<dl class="gloss">
<dt>POSITIONS</dt><dd>Record of your decisions, one entry each, such as P-37.</dd>
<dt>FACTS</dt><dd>Record of what is established about the repository's tree, one entry each, such as F-293.</dd>
<dt>record</dt><dd>Files in which the coordinator keeps what the project has decided and established, such as POSITIONS and FACTS.</dd>
<dt>history file</dt><dd>File beside POSITIONS or FACTS. It keeps every earlier text of an entry and why the text changed.</dd>
<dt>coordinator</dt><dd>Coordinating session.</dd>
<dt>worker</dt><dd>Agent that the coordinator launches.</dd>
<dt>Sonnet, Opus and Fable</dt><dd>Model tiers.</dd>
<dt>compaction</dt><dd>Replacement of the session's context with a summary.</dd>
<dt>boot</dt><dd>Session's start-up reading after a compaction.</dd>
<dt>page</dt><dd>Web page that the coordinator publishes for you to read and comment on.</dd>
</dl>
